[about]
Title=04 - Open a Folder and Find a File
Intro=A folder as a list: arrowing it, jumping to a file by name with Jump, and opening what you find. This walk assumes walks one to three.
Setup=FileDir is open on a folder of saved web pages.
Homework=Open a folder of your own, jump to a file by its first letters, and open it.

[step]

Say=Every folder opens as a list you arrow through. the reader says the folder and how many items are in it.
Key=
Hear=FileDir
Hear=List box C:\PodcastDirectories
Hear=119 items
Note=The count comes once, when the folder opens.

[step]

Say=Up and Down Arrows move through the list; a letter jumps to the first name starting with it. Enter on a folder goes in; Backspace comes back up.
Key=DownArrow
Hear=Blind Movers dot h t m

[step]

Say=Control plus J jumps to a file by name. FileDir asks for the text and remembers your last ten answers.
Key=Control+J
Hear=Jump
Hear=Text edit combo
Note=The window is named Jump because the key is J.

[step]

Say=Type access and press Enter.
Key=Enter
Hear=Access On dot h t m
Note=Jump looks at names. Control plus K looks inside the files.

[step]

Say=What this walk taught. I say the key; the reader says what it does.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Control plus J.
Key=
Hear=Jump
